From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:17:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panda: after_block_exec hook after the PC is synchronized

cpu_tb_exec ended the vCPU's pending block (panda_callbacks_after_block_exec) before
synchronize_from_tb. When a TB exits at its entry (an interrupt or icount expiry pending), the
block before it ran to its end, but without CF_PCREL (mips, ppc, any page with a TCG hook) chained
code had not stored the PC, so that block's after_block_exec saw a stale one. Run the hook
after the PC is synchronized. No change without --enable-panda (an empty inline).

SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Origin: new
---
 accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
index 6d3a4730f202aa30690870c52a580b35a3956eb0..104366dd076df3bb657fc91e30dbd6b6a60a170e 100644
--- a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
@@ -470,7 +470,6 @@ cpu_tb_exec(CPUState *cpu, TranslationBlock *itb, int *tb_exit)
     last_tb = tcg_splitwx_to_rw((void *)(ret & ~TB_EXIT_MASK));
     *tb_exit = ret & TB_EXIT_MASK;
 
-    panda_callbacks_after_block_exec(cpu, itb, *tb_exit);
     trace_exec_tb_exit(last_tb, *tb_exit);
 
     if (*tb_exit > TB_EXIT_IDX1) {
@@ -498,6 +497,12 @@ cpu_tb_exec(CPUState *cpu, TranslationBlock *itb, int *tb_exit)
         }
     }
 
+    /*
+     * PANDA: after the PC is synchronized above. A TB that exited at its entry
+     * never started; without CF_PCREL, chained code left the PC stale until then.
+     */
+    panda_callbacks_after_block_exec(cpu, itb, *tb_exit);
+
     /*
      * If gdb single-step, and we haven't raised another exception,
      * raise a debug exception.  Single-step with another exception
